<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henri Matisse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1869">1869</a>–<a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Matisse</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henri Matisse was a French painter, one of the leading figures of modern art in the twentieth century. Along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Picasso</a> and others, he admired African art that reached European collections. The site cites this admiration in discussing how the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-bronzes">Benin Bronzes</a> influenced European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modernism">modernism</a>, part of the legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henri-matisse.jpg" alt="Henri Matisse" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alvin Langdon Coburn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henri_Matisse,_1913,_photograph_by_Alvin_Langdon_Coburn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
